the dark knight is a beacon of hope  literally in one of the most goosebump  inducing scenes from the batman and fans  can't stop talking about it warning  spoilers for the batman ahead the batman  is darker than any previous iteration of  the mask vigilante's story with variety  describing it as a grounded frequently  brutal film noir  total film magazine quoted director matt  reeves as calling his movie the scariest  batman movie yet and critics and  audiences seem to agree  one element adding to the movie's dark  tone is the way batman is treated by  citizens of gotham  at best they're wary of him two years  into his career as a crime fighter he's  not exactly seen as a superhero not even  the christopher nolan movies made the  batman seem like such a threat to  regular people this is made clear at the  start of the film when on halloween  night a gang of thugs beat up on a man  riding public transportation when batman  swoops into a subway station to meet out  his personal brand of justice he lays  the bad guys out with ruthless  efficiency but then instead of being  grateful the victim cowers and asks  batman not to hurt him the scene  establishes batman as a frightening  force for everyone not just the bad guys  that's the way it stays for most of the  movie with comparisons being drawn  between the supposedly heroic batman and  the supposedly villainous riddler but  that all starts to change at the end of  the film with a scene that's giving fans  goosebumps and for good reason  fear is a tool  this goosebumps-inducing scene takes  place at the very end of the film batman  has failed in his efforts to contain the  riddler's damage not realizing until too  late that the criminal has placed  explosives at seven of gotham's sea  walls when they go off water floods the  city including gotham square garden  where the mayor elect bella real is  giving a victory speech to a crowd full  of gotham's most important people  batman soars in to save everyone but  before he does that he has to deal with  the internet army that the riddler has  put together who are on hand to make  sure the villain's plan goes smoothly in  the aftermath a number of people are  trapped by the collapsed building so  batman goes to rescue them at first they  are hesitant to accept batman's help not  knowing his motives the first to take  batman's offered hand is the young son  of former mayor don mitchell jr orphan  bruce wayne sees a bit of himself in the  boy whose father was killed at the start  of the film a young woman tentatively  follows eventually everyone lets him  lead them out of there through the  flooding waters batman ignites a red  flare and holds it up to light the way  becoming a literal beacon of hope  i'm vengeance the scene is part of the  character's own journey in the film  batman starts out moodily telling his  enemies that he's the personification of  vengeance later one of the riddler's  cronies says the same about himself when  batman asks him why he's helping to  cause such terror in the city at that  point batman realizes how much in common  he has with the bad guys and it prompts  him to reflect on his mission and what  he wants to stand for at the end of the  movie bruce realizes that he can't just  stand for vengeance he has to be a  symbol of hope this scene coupled with  bruce's emotional growth allows the film  to end on a somber yet optimistic note  posters on reddit discuss the scene in  detail with one user on reddit praising  the hard-hitting theme they wrote this  was a pivotal concept that batman had to  confront in order to find a sense of  justice built on something more stable  than anger and vengeance batman needs to  be fear but he also must be hope another  user on reddit gave their thumbs up as  well writing the whole character arc of  the batman from the vengeance to hope  was showcased masterfully one user on  reddit thought the scene was meaningful  and visually beautiful writing that  scene when he's helping the people in  the flooded area and leading them to a  safe place is just beautiful visually  and story wise perfect depiction of  batman being the beacon of hope it makes  sense that batman would be facing this  character development at this early  stage of his career as a caped crime  fighter naturally a city facing such  rampant crime would be suspicious of a  masked interloper diving in to take  matters into his own hands  after dealing with the threat of the  riddler however the people of gotham and  batman himself have a better idea of  what he's actually trying to accomplish  justice  the answer's justice  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the batman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

